WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:05.460
- Hi, I'm Meagan from Khan Academy.

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:06.420
And in this video,

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:10.183
we're gonna explore Khan
Academy's course mastery system.

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:14.580
At Khan Academy we're
devoted to mastery learning,

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:18.100
and build our content around
our course mastery system.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:21.170
However, a question we hear
frequently from teachers is,

00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:24.943
what exactly do we mean by
course mastery on Khan Academy?

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:28.370
Course mastery on Khan Academy,

00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:30.020
is a feature that allows teachers

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:33.330
to set and track long term
learning goals for students,

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:36.163
while encouraging students
to work at their own pace.

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:39.220
Currently course mastery is available

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:41.840
for courses with full practice content.

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:44.580
All of our math courses
including AP Calculus,

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:47.350
AB, BC, AP Statistics

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:49.650
and our Get Ready for grade level courses,

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:53.140
as well as Grammar, High
School Biology, AP Biology,

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:56.470
AP Physics 1, US government and civics,

00:00:56.470 --> 00:01:00.950
AP US government and politics,
US History, AP US history,

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:05.040
World History Project
Origins, AP macroeconomics,

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:07.750
Microeconomics, AP Microeconomics,

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:10.083
and AP Computer Science Principles.

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:14.710
Assigning course mastery goals,

00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:18.060
allows teachers to set
and track long term goals.

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:18.900
Let's walk through

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:22.600
how to assign course mastery
goals to your students.

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:24.150
When you log in to Khan Academy,

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:26.840
you'll land on the teacher dashboard.

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:28.340
Click on the name of the class,

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:30.040
you want to assign a mastery goal.

00:01:31.510 --> 00:01:34.000
On the left hand side navigation,

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:36.403
go to the course mastery placement tab,

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:39.140
if you haven't done so already,

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:41.970
at the on grade level
course you currently teach.

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:43.660
And if you're a math teacher,

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:46.570
add to get ready for grade level course.

00:01:46.570 --> 00:01:48.610
If you're about to start the school year,

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:51.530
we recommend assigning the get
ready for grade level course,

00:01:51.530 --> 00:01:52.820
as a course mastery goal,

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:54.560
to have students begin the year,

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:57.090
by gap filling and
strengthening fundamentals,

00:01:57.090 --> 00:01:59.960
before diving into on grade level skills.

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:02.670
For example, if I were
a 5th grade teacher,

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:03.590
I would start the year

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:06.333
by signing the get ready
for fifth grade course.

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:11.460
Click the blue button, add these courses.

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:14.510
Now you'll be on the course
mastery placement page.

00:02:14.510 --> 00:02:16.470
Click assign goal,

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:19.870
you can confirm your assign
the desired goals to students,

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:21.990
by selecting course mastery placement

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:23.900
on the left-hand panel,

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:26.120
and you will now see the
current mastery goals,

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:28.033
assigned to students in your class.

00:02:30.656 --> 00:02:32.650
A students work on Khan Academy.

00:02:32.650 --> 00:02:34.500
You can also add additional courses,

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:38.093
for students to work on, either
below or above grade level.

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:43.110
You can assign the same course
for all students to master,

00:02:43.110 --> 00:02:44.730
or you can assign different courses

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:47.880
to individuals or groups of students.

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:50.410
We recommend using Khan
Academy's skill report,

00:02:50.410 --> 00:02:52.870
to look more closely at students progress,

00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:56.393
and determine the best goal,
or goals for each student.

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:01.840
Now let's look a little closer

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:05.053
at what students see in terms
of course mastery goals.

00:03:06.210 --> 00:03:08.490
When students log in to Khan Academy,

00:03:08.490 --> 00:03:10.770
they will view on their learner home page,

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:13.280
each student will be able
to see their teacher,

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:16.020
or class name on the left hand side.

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:17.570
By clicking on the class,

00:03:17.570 --> 00:03:19.880
students will see their mastery goal.

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:22.120
A student can click the goal at any time,

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:24.170
and continue from where they left off,

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:26.860
to make progress towards their goal.

00:03:26.860 --> 00:03:29.780
Students can continue working
toward their mastery goal,

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:32.453
on the iOS and Android apps as well.

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:37.987
Every skill or concept has
multiple mastery levels,

00:03:37.987 --> 00:03:41.840
and students earn additional
points, with each new level.

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:44.840
There are several ways
for students to practice,

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:48.630
they can practice a single
concept at a time on an exercise,

00:03:48.630 --> 00:03:51.280
or they can practice a
mix of different concepts,

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:55.630
on a quiz, unit test, course
challenge or mastery challenge.

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:57.370
As students get questions right,

00:03:57.370 --> 00:04:01.110
they move up from not started,
to familiar, to proficient,

00:04:01.110 --> 00:04:02.793
the top level is mastered.

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:05.810
Students can only get to mastered,

00:04:05.810 --> 00:04:07.140
by getting to proficient,

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:10.150
and then getting that concept
right, on a unit test,

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:12.363
course challenge, or mastery challenge.

00:04:13.301 --> 00:04:14.610
Most teachers recommend,

00:04:14.610 --> 00:04:16.800
having students start
with the course challenge,

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:19.720
or specific unit tests within the course.

00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:21.670
This way both students and teachers,

00:04:21.670 --> 00:04:23.310
can quickly identify gaps

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:25.320
and strengths in student knowledge,

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:27.450
in order to provide the right content,

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:29.653
and right support in the right moment.

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:33.730
When students are stuck
or missed questions,

00:04:33.730 --> 00:04:35.710
their mastery level moves down,

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:37.780
and a symbol appears next to the concept,

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:40.690
to help them remember where to focus.

00:04:40.690 --> 00:04:42.920
If students are consistently
missing problems

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:45.920
about a concept, they'll
move to attempted status,

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:49.360
and a red dot will appear
next to that concept.

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:51.340
Mastery of individual concepts,

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:53.000
contributes to unit progress,

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:55.023
and to overall course progress.

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:58.900
A mastery goal is considered achieved,

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:01.890
once a student reaches 90% mastery,

00:05:01.890 --> 00:05:05.263
though they can still access
previous goals, at any time.

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:08.860
Students can always see
what they've completed,

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:10.970
and what they should work on next.

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:14.590
Additionally, once students
have begun working in a course,

00:05:14.590 --> 00:05:16.310
they will receive mastery challenges,

00:05:16.310 --> 00:05:18.460
which appear at the
top of the course page.

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:21.770
Mastery challenges,
highlight opportunities

00:05:21.770 --> 00:05:22.900
for students to engage

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:26.020
in personalized spaced
repetition of the skills,

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:28.163
students have already started practicing.

00:05:29.150 --> 00:05:32.040
Research shows that
spiraling skills over time,

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:33.420
and across lessons,

00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:36.610
is a key component to minimizing
student learning loss,

00:05:36.610 --> 00:05:38.583
and improving knowledge retention.

00:05:42.370 --> 00:05:45.550
We'll be diving deeper into
reports, in a later lesson.

00:05:45.550 --> 00:05:46.870
But let's take a quick look,

00:05:46.870 --> 00:05:49.663
at where to find mastery
progress, for students.

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:54.880
Starting at the teacher
dashboard, select a class,

00:05:54.880 --> 00:05:58.700
select course mastery progress,
from the left-hand panel.

00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:02.580
This report shows student
progress on the selected course.

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:04.250
First you'll see class progress,

00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:06.510
towards overall course mastery,

00:06:06.510 --> 00:06:09.970
and the median mastery
for the class as a whole.

00:06:09.970 --> 00:06:13.310
Below, you'll see the
mastery for each unit,

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:15.060
perhaps it's the start of the year,

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:17.520
and you're focusing on this first unit.

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:19.310
By clicking on any unit,

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:21.750
you can see the additional
detail of progress,

00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:24.010
for each student at the unit level,

00:06:24.010 --> 00:06:26.560
including each student's mastery progress,

00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:28.530
for that unit, and the class median,

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:30.423
for unit mastery progress.

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:34.670
Khan Academy also has a skills report,

00:06:34.670 --> 00:06:36.820
found under the activity overview,

00:06:36.820 --> 00:06:39.170
to dive deeper into the individual skills

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:41.100
for a given course.

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:43.900
On the skills report,
you can open any unit,

00:06:43.900 --> 00:06:46.420
to get a quick view of how
students are progressing,

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:48.000
for the skills in that unit,

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:50.693
by looking at the purple
bars on the right side.

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:53.800
By clicking on a specific skill,

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:55.890
you will be able to see the mastery level,

00:06:55.890 --> 00:06:58.630
for every student for that skill.

00:06:58.630 --> 00:06:59.463
If you notice

00:06:59.463 --> 00:07:01.890
that several students are
struggling on a skill,

00:07:01.890 --> 00:07:04.710
you can assign extra
practice on that skill,

00:07:04.710 --> 00:07:06.513
right here in the skills report.

00:07:07.890 --> 00:07:09.930
We'll talk more about
how to make assignments,

00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:11.053
in a separate video.

00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:13.580
Some advice from teachers

00:07:13.580 --> 00:07:16.683
using Khan Academy's course
mastery in their classrooms.

00:07:17.640 --> 00:07:20.910
Mastering an entire course,
can feel daunting to students,

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:24.520
so break it up into
checkpoints, like monthly goals.

00:07:24.520 --> 00:07:26.780
You can also consider
having students focus,

00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:29.220
on particular units throughout the year.

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:32.660
Then check the unit report,
to see how they're doing.

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:34.180
Also you don't need to assign

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:36.840
the same course mastery
goal, to every student.

00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:39.570
To differentiate, you can
assign different courses

00:07:39.570 --> 00:07:41.290
to different students.

00:07:41.290 --> 00:07:43.550
Some teachers even assign a mastery goal

00:07:43.550 --> 00:07:44.980
for a previous grade level,

00:07:44.980 --> 00:07:47.570
as review at the start of the year.

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:49.560
We hope this video helps you get started,

00:07:49.560 --> 00:07:51.853
using course mastery with your students.

